@@ -2060,3 +2060,10 @@ legacy tests.
 | SCENARIO-VERIFY-5300 | Misleading Assumptions Are Blocked By The Instance-Class Gate | Implemented | Artifact follows bounded CPU replay using deterministic Exp5292 and Exp5299 fixtures, blocks misleading_factor_sat, misleading_repair, and semantic_wrong_control before unsafe p-bit assumptions can route, preserves solver-authoritative SAT/UNSAT correctness, and records gated aggregate conflicts 15 versus ungated 18 and solver-only 24 (conflicts_saved_by_gate=3; solver_only_vs_gated conflicts_saved=9). Tests_run remains pending final verification in the artifact, so no additional test-pass claim is made; no hardware speedup, retro closure, AUC/TP/FP/signed_improvement, or violation_rate metric is claimed. |
 | REQ-INFER-5301 | EBT Spectral Step-Control Stability Diagnostic | Implemented | `python/carnot/experiment_5301_ebt_spectral_step_control_diagnostic_v484.py`; `tests/python/test_experiment_5301_ebt_spectral_step_control_diagnostic_v484.py`; `openspec/capabilities/llm-ebm-inference/spec.md`; `results/experiment_5301_ebt_spectral_step_control_diagnostic_v484.json`; honest_verdict={"principle":"Terminal Exp 5301 verdict; starts with complete:, null:, or blocked_ and states whether spectral step-control is usable.","value":"complete: spectral step-control is usable as a tiny deterministic stability diagnostic before energy-guided inner-loop claims"}; status=<missing>; spectral_control_ready.value=true; adaptive_recovered=true; adaptive_total_recovery_shrinks=8; aggressive_diverged=true; aggressive_divergence_step=0; adaptive_final_energy=0.227619159308; aggressive_final_energy=200.687772; no retro_* flags; no AUC/TP/FP/signed_improvement/violation_rate fields; no LLM decoding, SOTA, GPU, hardware speedup, or language-quality claim is made. |
 | SCENARIO-INFER-5301 | Spectral Control Recovers Where Aggressive Fixed Step Diverges | Implemented | Artifact follows an offline deterministic continuous-energy fixture: the aggressive fixed policy diverges at step 0 with final_energy=200.687772, while adaptive spectral control estimates lambda_max around 100, shrinks eight accepted steps to alpha=0.012, recovers without divergence, and reaches final_energy=0.227619159308 from initial_energy=51.33. The claim is limited to a tiny stability diagnostic before energy-guided inner-loop work; no retro closure, AUC/TP/FP/signed_improvement, violation_rate, LLM decoding, quality, hardware, or speedup claim is recorded. |
+| REQ-LEARN-5302 | Adaptive Memory Policy Self-Learning Harness | Implemented | `python/carnot/experiment_5302_adaptive_memory_policy_self_learning_v484.py`; `tests/python/test_experiment_5302_adaptive_memory_policy_self_learning_v484.py`; `openspec/capabilities/self-learning/spec.md`; `results/experiment_5302_adaptive_memory_policy_self_learning_v484.json`; honest_verdict={"principle":"Terminal Exp 5302 verdict; starts with complete:, null:, harmful_, or blocked_ and states whether the adaptive memory policy helped on held-out deterministic cases.","value":"complete: adaptive memory policy helped; held-out quality matched always-full, avoided 3/7 full verifier calls and kept unsafe_false_accepts=0 without weight mutation"}; status=<missing>; adaptive_memory_policy_positive.value=true; memory_policy_candidate_ready=true; heldout_quality_delta_vs_always_full.value delta=0.0; full_verifier_calls_avoided.value vs_always_full=3 rate_vs_always_full=0.428571; unsafe_false_accepts.value.count=0; no_weight_mutation.value=true; no retro_* flags; no AUC/TP/FP/signed_improvement/violation_rate fields. |
+| REQ-LEARN-5302-1 | Selection And Held-Out Splits Are Disjoint | Implemented | Artifact records split_summary.case_ids_disjoint=true with six selection rows and seven held-out rows; held-out case IDs were not seen during policy selection. |
+| REQ-LEARN-5302-2 | Unsafe And Conflicting Memory Controls Escalate Or Reject | Implemented | Artifact records stale_conflict_behavior.all_escalated=true, rollback_exercised.value.trigger_count=2, rejected_promotions=7, false_accepts.count=0, and unsafe_false_accepts.value.count=0 across stale, contradictory, shuffled, harmful-memory, rollback, unsupported, and format-invalid held-out controls. |
+| REQ-LEARN-5302-3 | Result Reports Quality, Call Avoidance, And False Accepts | Implemented | Artifact records adaptive and always-full held-out quality rates both 1.0 with delta=0.0, adaptive full_verifier_calls=4 versus always_full=7, full_verifier_calls_avoided.value vs_always_full=3 at rate_vs_always_full=0.428571, and false_accepts.count=0. |
+| REQ-LEARN-5302-4 | Policy State Records Reversible Memory And Counters | Implemented | Artifact records policy_version=`adaptive-memory-policy-v5302-selection-threshold-v1`, optimized_on_split=`selection`, confidence_threshold=0.84, one promoted memory entry, seven rejected promotions, counters blocked_controls=4 heldout_cases=7 retrievals=2 rollbacks=2 selection_cases=6, and reversible no-weight-mutation policy state. |
+| REQ-LEARN-5302-5 | No Weight Mutation Gate Is Explicit | Implemented | Artifact records no_weight_mutation.value=true and adaptive_policy_state_after_heldout.no_weight_mutation=true, limiting the self-learning claim to reversible policy counters, memory entries, retrieval choices, and thresholds rather than model-weight updates. |
+| SCENARIO-LEARN-5302 | Adaptive Memory Policy Is Selected On Selection Rows And Tested Held-Out | Implemented | Artifact follows the bounded deterministic no-weight-mutation path using Exp5275, Exp5285, Exp5289, and Exp5290 inputs; it selects threshold 0.84 on selection rows, tests on seven disjoint held-out rows, preserves always-full quality, avoids 3/7 full verifier calls with one additional avoided call versus no-memory and fixed-governed-memory baselines, keeps unsafe_false_accepts.value.count=0, exercises rollback twice, and sets honest_verdict.value to `complete: adaptive memory policy helped; held-out quality matched always-full, avoided 3/7 full verifier calls and kept unsafe_false_accepts=0 without weight mutation`. Tests_run remains pending artifact bootstrap before final rerun in the artifact, so no additional test-pass claim is made. |
